{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-generated-f9cd3011a4607c23","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"In the lambda calculus, an expression (λx. M) N is a β-redex: λx. M is a function with parameter x, and N is the argument supplied to it. Reducing it replaces occurrences of x that refer to this function parameter, except occurrences inside a nested λx binding, with N. Before replacing, rename nested parameters when necessary so that variables inside N do not accidentally become bound; this capture-avoiding replacement is written M[N/x].","requires":["lambda calculus","variable binding"],"citationRequired":false}]}]}
